    93	
    94	### 3.3 Broken companions: every one RED
    95	
    96	There are two kinds of run per companion:
    97	
    98	- An all-invariants run, which stops at the first violation.
    99	- A **per-invariant matrix**: 32 single-invariant runs in each instance, which gives the exact red set.
   100	
   101	**All 14 matrices (7 companions × 2 instances) match their predicted red sets exactly**: no extra reds, none
   102	missing, no TLC errors. Every green matrix run covered the full 7,938 or 15,876 states.
   103	
   104	| Companion (defect) | First red (all-invariants run, V1) | Exact red set (V1; General identical unless noted) |
   105	|---|---|---|
   106	| **FailOpen.** An unknown alg is treated as passed, and its opaque signature is accepted. **This is the registered A3.6.2 item 3 companion.** | `UnknownAlgGivesUnverifiable`. Counterexample: kms supported/good, gpg **unsupported/bad**, evidence good → the broken verifier says `VALID_STRICT` | `UnknownAlgGivesUnverifiable`, **`UnknownAlgNeverValid`**, `AlgUnknownReasonExact`, `ExactUnverifiableIn`, `ExactStrictIn` (5). General adds `ExactDegradedIn` (6) |
   107	| **MalformedAsUnknown.** Every non-supported id form is treated as unknown | `InvalidAlgFormsGiveInvalid` (gpg alg *missing* → `UNVERIFIABLE`) | `InvalidAlgFormsGiveInvalid`, `AlgUnknownReasonExact`, `MixedFailedUnknownInvalid`, `MixedFailedMissingEvidenceInvalid`, `ExactInvalidIn`, `ExactUnverifiableIn` (6) |
   108	| **MissingSigAsEvidence.** An absent signature is treated as unperformable | `MixedFailedMissingEvidenceInvalid` (both signatures and both evidence members absent → `UNVERIFIABLE`) | `AlgUnknownReasonExact`, `MixedFailedUnknownInvalid`, `MixedFailedMissingEvidenceInvalid`, **`MissingSignatureInvalid`**, `ExactInvalidIn`, `ExactUnverifiableIn` (6) |
   109	| **MissingEvidenceAsFail.** Absent evidence is treated as a failure | `MissingEvidenceUnverifiable` (evidence absent, all else good → `INVALID`) | `UnknownAlgGivesUnverifiable`, **`MissingEvidenceUnverifiable`**, `InvalidNeedsDefect`, `ExactInvalidIn`, `ExactUnverifiableIn` (5) |
   110	| **UnknownDominates.** An unknown alg overrides A4.2 precedence (the shape of Codex finding 11) | `AlgUnknownReasonExact` (unknown alg plus absent signatures → `UNVERIFIABLE / ALG_UNKNOWN`) | `InvalidAlgFormsGiveInvalid`, `KnownAlgBadSigInvalid`, `AlgUnknownReasonExact`, **`MixedFailedUnknownInvalid`**, `MixedFailedMissingEvidenceInvalid`, `MissingSignatureInvalid`, `MissingEvidenceUnverifiable`, `ExactInvalidIn`, `ExactUnverifiableIn`, `AgreesWithP4` (10) |
   111	| **UnknownAsOutOfProfile.** An in-profile unknown alg is handled as a terminal dispatch rejection | `OutOfProfileOnlyAtDispatch` | The 10 above, plus `OutOfProfileOnlyAtDispatch` (11) |
   112	| **DispatchFallthrough.** Out-of-profile input is evaluated anyway | `DispatchTerminal` (dispatch out → evaluated) | **`DispatchTerminal`**, `AlgUnknownReasonExact`, `InvalidNeedsDefect` (3) |
   113	
   114	**Finding: P4 alone is blind to all five classification defects.** For FailOpen, MalformedAsUnknown,
   115	MissingSigAsEvidence and MissingEvidenceAsFail, all eleven `P4_*` formulas stay green, and so does `AgreesWithP4`.
   116	For UnknownDominates and UnknownAsOutOfProfile, the eleven `P4_*` formulas stay green. The defect sits in how inputs
   117	become check outcomes, upstream of the function P4 checks. This is why E6a's invariants are stated over the raw
   118	inputs rather than the status map.
