docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-433-1. **Past receipts survive later compromise.** A receipt whose exact signatures are anchored by T cannot have
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-434-   signatures manufactured after an adversary gains signing capability for every required slot substituted into
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-435-   it, while SHA-256, the OTS commitment and the pinned chain history stay secure. Its historical authenticity also
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-436-   needs the signing and key-use assumptions to have held before T, authentic historical authority, and no relevant
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-437-   compromise before T; V1 does not evaluate these (`historical_security: NOT_EVALUATED`). A later key theft or
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-438-   algorithm break does not by itself invalidate such a receipt. It does not cure earlier theft, unauthorized
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-439-   signing before T, misissuance or whole-author-sphere capture, and does not prove that the issuer itself obtained
docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md-440-   the stamp or issued the bundle uniquely.
